IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpula-practice`

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (Western Australia) -- legal costs: what a legal costs determination of the
-- Legal Costs Committee may cover (ss 3, 132-134), when it comes into force and must be reviewed (ss 137, 140, 299), what it
-- governs and what displaces it -- including a costs agreement made under the Uniform Law (s 141) -- the law practice's added
-- disclosure duty (s 143), and the review of, and recovery after, a costs assessment (ss 149, 151).
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 47480, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47480.txt; see lpula-practice.l4 for the compilation table.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement au/wa:REQ-0012 (priority 1), raised 3 times by the Western Australian cradle-to-grave life of
-- Daniel. This module answers what this Act says about d038 (2029-03-04, aged 32): Daniel "Acts for a client in an arbitration under
-- a conditional costs agreement with a 25% uplift"; "Is a conditional costs agreement lawful; what is prohibited; is the arbitration
-- agreement binding?". The ledger cites Uniform Law ss 181 (conditional costs agreements) and 183 (contingency fees prohibited).
-- Those sections are in the Uniform Law (subject legal-profession-uniform-law-wa, au/wa:REQ-0033), not in this Act. Whether a costs
-- agreement complies with the Law's Part 4.3 Division 4 -- including whether a 25% uplift is permitted -- is an INPUT here. The
-- arbitration agreement is a question for the Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (a separate subject).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the content of any costs determination (rates and amounts are set by the Committee and are INPUTS); costs assessment
-- procedure (ss 144-148, 152) beyond ss 149 and 151; the interest rate under s 150(3) (set under the Civil Judgments Enforcement Act
-- 2004 s 8(1)(a); an INPUT); the Legal Aid Commission rules (s 146); the Civil Liability Act 2002 s 15L and the Motor Vehicle
-- (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 s 27A, which the s 141 note mentions.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (WA) -- legal costs`

§§ `helpers`

-- Days since a fixed origin for a YYYYMMDD date (proleptic Gregorian calendar), so that two dates can be subtracted.
GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`shifted year of` MEANS
    IF `month of` `d` AT MOST 2 THEN `year of` `d` MINUS 1 ELSE `year of` `d`

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`year of era of` MEANS `shifted year of` `d` MINUS FLOOR (`shifted year of` `d` DIVIDED BY 400) TIMES 400

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`day of shifted year of` MEANS
    FLOOR ((153 TIMES ((`month of` `d` PLUS 9) MODULO 12) PLUS 2) DIVIDED BY 5) PLUS `day of` `d` MINUS 1

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`day number of` MEANS
    FLOOR (`shifted year of` `d` DIVIDED BY 400) TIMES 146097
    PLUS `year of era of` `d` TIMES 365
    PLUS FLOOR (`year of era of` `d` DIVIDED BY 4)
    MINUS FLOOR (`year of era of` `d` DIVIDED BY 100)
    PLUS `day of shifted year of` `d`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` MEANS `day number of` `b` MINUS `day number of` `a`

§§ `3, 132-134 -- what a costs determination may cover`

-- s 3: "contentious business means legal services by an Australian legal practitioner in or for the purposes of any action, suit or
-- proceedings before a court, but does not include the administration of estates and trusts"; "noncontentious business means legal
-- services other than contentious business".
-- s 132: "In this Division -- court includes an arbitrator, a tribunal or a person, with the power to require the production of
-- documents or the answering of questions."
-- s 133(1): the Legal Costs Committee "may make legal costs determinations regulating the costs that may be charged by law practices
-- in respect of -- (a) noncontentious business; and (b) contentious business before -- (i) the Supreme Court; or (ii) the District
-- Court; or (iii) the Magistrates Court; or (iv) a court of summary jurisdiction; or (v) the State Administrative Tribunal; or (vi)
-- the Family Court of Western Australia; or (vii) any other court declared by the Attorney General under section 134(1)".
--
-- FORK. Work in an arbitration. If "court" in the s 3 definition of contentious business keeps its ordinary meaning, an arbitration
-- is not a proceeding before a court, the work is noncontentious business, and s 133(1)(a) covers it. If s 132 ("In this Division")
-- is read into contentious business where Division 1 uses it, the arbitration is contentious business before a "court" that s
-- 133(1)(b) does not list, and a determination covers it only if the Attorney General has declared it under s 134(1). The text does
-- not settle which; both readings are encoded and asserted.
DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `no proceedings`
    `the Supreme Court`
    `the District Court`
    `the Magistrates Court`
    `the State Administrative Tribunal`
    `the Family Court of Western Australia`
    `an arbitrator`
    `the Federal Court of Australia`

GIVEN `the forum` IS A Forum, `estates or trusts administration` IS A BOOLEAN, `reading s 132 into contentious business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is contentious business` IF
        (NOT `estates or trusts administration`)
    AND CONSIDER `the forum`
        WHEN `no proceedings` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an arbitrator` THEN `reading s 132 into contentious business`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the forum` IS A Forum
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the forum is listed in s 133(1)(b)` IF
    CONSIDER `the forum`
    WHEN `the Supreme Court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the District Court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Magistrates Court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the State Administrative Tribunal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Family Court of Western Australia` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the forum` IS A Forum, `estates or trusts administration` IS A BOOLEAN, `reading s 132 into contentious business` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared under s 134(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a costs determination may cover the work` IF
    IF `the work is contentious business` `the forum` `estates or trusts administration` `reading s 132 into contentious business`
    THEN `the forum is listed in s 133(1)(b)` `the forum` OR `declared under s 134(1)`
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `137, 140, 299 -- force and review of a determination`

-- s 140(3): a costs determination "comes into force on -- (a) the day on which the report of the determination is published under
-- subsection (2); or (b) if a later day is specified in the report -- that day."
GIVEN `published on` IS A NUMBER, `a later day is specified` IS A BOOLEAN, `the specified day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the determination comes into force on` MEANS
    IF `a later day is specified` AND `the specified day` GREATER THAN `published on`
    THEN `the specified day`
    ELSE `published on`

-- s 137(1): the Committee "must review each costs determination in force -- (a) at least once in the period of 2 years beginning on
-- the day on which it was made; and (b) at least once in each subsequent 2-year period."
-- s 299(2), (3): an old-Act determination (old Act s 275(1)) is "taken, on and from commencement day, to be a legal costs determination
-- made under section 133(1)" and, for s 137(1), "is taken to be made on the day on which it was made under the old Act".
-- The 2-year period beginning on day D is taken to end the day before the second anniversary of D.
GIVEN `made on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first review period ends before` MEANS `months after` `made on` 24

GIVEN `made on` IS A NUMBER, `reviewed since made` IS A BOOLEAN, `today` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first s 137 review is overdue` IF
        (NOT `reviewed since made`)
    AND `today` AT LEAST `the first review period ends before` `made on`

§§ `141 -- what a determination governs, and what displaces it`

-- s 141(1): "The following are regulated by an applicable costs determination -- (a) the taxation of bills of law practices; (b) any
-- other aspect of the costs charged by law practices."
-- (2): "Subsection (1) is subject to -- (a) any costs agreement made in accordance with the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) Part 4.3
-- Division 4 or the corresponding provision of a corresponding law; and (b) section 146; and (c) the Legal Aid Commission Act 1976
-- section 14."
-- (3): a court or judicial officer who thinks the determination's amount "inadequate because of the unusual difficulty, complexity
-- or importance of the matter" may order costs above it, fix higher limits or remove limits.
-- Part 4.3 Division 4 of the Law (costs agreements; the ledger cites its ss 181, conditional costs agreements, and 183, contingency
-- fees) is not deposited here. Whether the agreement was made in accordance with it is an INPUT. A costs
-- agreement that was not so made does not displace the determination under s 141(2)(a); what else follows for it is for the Law.
DECLARE `Costs matter` HAS
    `an applicable costs determination exists` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a costs agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement complies with Uniform Law Part 4.3 Division 4` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Legal Aid Commission Act s 14 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a court found the determination inadequate for unusual difficulty, complexity or importance` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Costs matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the costs agreement displaces the determination` IF
        `the matter`'s `there is a costs agreement`
    AND `the matter`'s `the agreement complies with Uniform Law Part 4.3 Division 4`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Costs matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the costs determination governs the costs` IF
        `the matter`'s `an applicable costs determination exists`
    AND (NOT `the costs agreement displaces the determination` `the matter`)
    AND (NOT `the matter`'s `Legal Aid Commission Act s 14 applies`)
    AND (NOT `the matter`'s `a court found the determination inadequate for unusual difficulty, complexity or importance`)

§§ `143 -- disclosure`

-- s 143: "When a law practice provides a client with information under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) section 174(1)(a), the law
-- practice must provide the client with information about whether the legal costs are subject to a costs determination."
GIVEN `gave s 174(1)(a) information` IS A BOOLEAN, `said whether a costs determination applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the law practice breached s 143` IF
    `gave s 174(1)(a) information` AND (NOT `said whether a costs determination applies`)

§§ `149, 151 -- after a costs assessment`

-- s 149(1), (2): a party "may apply to the Supreme Court for a review of the assessment"; the application "must be made -- (a) within
-- 28 days after the day on which the party is notified of the costs assessment". s 148: otherwise the assessment "is binding on all
-- parties ... and ... is not subject to appeal or review".
GIVEN `notified on` IS A NUMBER, `applied on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the review application is in time` IF
        `days from` `notified on` `applied on` AT LEAST 0
    AND `days from` `notified on` `applied on` AT MOST 28

-- s 151: "If a person paid an amount as legal costs and that amount exceeds the legal costs determined to be payable on a costs
-- assessment ... the excess amount is recoverable in a court of competent jurisdiction as a debt due to the person."
GIVEN `paid` IS A NUMBER, `assessed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess recoverable as a debt` MEANS
    IF `paid` GREATER THAN `assessed` THEN `paid` MINUS `assessed` ELSE 0
